30,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"We are losing key people and new hires take forever. Plus, standard training is being ignored at the depots.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Our yards are a mess of old gear, and trying to cut over during peak season is a disaster.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The board ignores operating costs but cuts capital. Also, separate licenses lead to price creep over time.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"We had a two-day outage because no one owned the problem. Also, our rules change too fast for frozen scopes.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"We've skipped upgrades because testing is too heavy, and external data migrations have left us with lasting errors.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Yumi, if no one owns the support, the overworked admins will be the ones suffering most.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, if the gear is old, does a fancy new system even matter if it can't talk to the yard?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Yumi, the ""frozen scope"" you mentioned is exactly why operating costs spike later to fix the gaps.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"Exactly. We need a vendor who doesn't just vanish after the initial setup is ""complete.""","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, that suggests we should avoid modular systems that allow for endless, expensive add-ons.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Misaki,,We can't afford a system that requires a massive retraining effort that the supervisors will just ignore.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Kenji,,And we can't have a rollout that ignores the November to January blackout. It's impossible.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"A fixed-price, bundled model seems safer for the budget than a modular one.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"I agree. We need a single point of accountability for support, not a finger-pointing match.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,I'm wary of external partners handling the data. We need someone who stays until it actually works.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
