55,3,1,talk,Misaki,,Candidate D has an engineering team present through rollout. That helps with the training gap.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Kenji,,D is built for transport operators. That might actually survive our yards and the peak season.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Toshio,,B is a hosted suite with a fixed configuration. That sounds more predictable than A's modular licensing.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"B has a regional service team, which solves the ownership issue. But D's on-site presence is better.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"C uses a partner for migration, which I distrust. D's on-site engineers are a stronger bet for stability.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Toshio, would D's on-premise model be a capital or operating expense?","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Yumi, do you think B's fixed configuration can handle the warehouse rule changes we keep seeing?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Toshio,,On-premise is usually capital. The board is trimming that. B's hosted model is an operating cost.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"I doubt B's ""fixed"" process can handle our volatility. D's engineers can adapt in real-time.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"D's specific focus on transport means less ""repair work"" later compared to a general suite like B or C.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I'm leaning toward D. Having the team there is the only way the supervisors will adopt it.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm with Misaki. D understands the industry and the physical constraints.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"I prefer B for the budget, but if D is the only one that works, the cost is irrelevant.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Yumi,,I'll go with D. On-site support is the best way to ensure accountability.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,D is the most logical choice to avoid the technical debt and migration failures of the past.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
